prompt_text_by_variant.B:
For the single stimulus word supplied by the user, freely generate the properties that come to mind. Aim for 10 different properties, including any physical or perceptual characteristics, uses or functions, and background facts that you associate with the concept.

Do not judge a supplied feature list and do not add repetitive filler. Return at most 10 properties, or fewer when appropriate.

Return only this JSON object, with no markdown or additional text:
{
  "target_word": "the supplied stimulus word",
  "features": [
    "one concise property",
    "another concise property"
  ]
}

prompt_text_by_variant.C:
You are completing a free feature-generation task for one stimulus word.

Before answering, consider the concept from several perspectives:
- what it looks, sounds, feels, tastes, or is physically made of;
- its functions: what it does, what it is used for, or how people interact with it;
- its category, typical setting, origins, associations, and other generally known facts.

Then select up to 10 of the clearest, most distinct properties that come to mind. Do not force a fixed number from each perspective, repeat the same idea, evaluate a supplied feature list, or invent a property merely to reach 10.

Return only one JSON object with exactly this structure:
{
  "target_word": "the supplied stimulus word",
  "features": [
    "one concise property",
    "another concise property"
  ]
}

Do not include reasoning, numbering, perspective labels, markdown, or text outside the JSON object.
